    "markdown": "---\ntitle: \"04. Newton's method: a loop that stops when it has converged\"\ndescription: \"Data-dependent control flow: differentiate through a while loop with a convergence test, and through the in-place Thomas sweeps inside it.\"\njupyter: python3\n---\n\n\n\n## The problem\n\nSolve the nonlinear boundary-value problem\n$$F(u, \\theta) = A u + u^3 - \\theta = 0, \\qquad A = \\tfrac{1}{h^2}\\operatorname{tridiag}(-1, 2, -1),$$\nby Newton's method **until** the step is small, $\\lVert\\delta\\rVert_\\infty \\le 10^{-10}\\lVert u\\rVert_\\infty$, and differentiate\n$\\mathcal{L}(\\theta) = \\lVert u^\\ast(\\theta) - u_{\\text{obs}}\\rVert^2$ with respect to\n$\\theta$. Each Newton step solves a tridiagonal system with the Thomas algorithm, a\nsequential in-place sweep.\n\nTwo irregular patterns:\n\n- **Data-dependent control flow.** The number of Newton steps depends on $\\theta$\n  (3–4 here).\n- **Sequential in-place update.** The Thomas forward elimination and back substitution.\n\n## Code\n\n::: {.panel-tabset group=\"impl\"}\n## Enzyme.jl\n{{< embed enzyme.qmd#loss echo=true >}}\n{{< embed enzyme.qmd#grad echo=true >}}\n\nImplicit-function alternative:\n{{< embed enzyme.qmd#grad-implicit echo=true >}}\n\n## JAX\n{{< embed jax.qmd#loss echo=true >}}\n{{< embed jax.qmd#grad echo=true >}}\n:::\n\nThe direct JAX translation, `jax.grad` of a `lax.while_loop`, is rejected:\nreverse mode needs a static trip count. JAX offers two ways out: run a fixed,\nworst-case number of steps, or switch to implicit differentiation (Optimistix). Enzyme\ndifferentiates the loop as written, and the implicit adjoint is still available as a\ntwo-line alternative.\n\n## Same gradient\n\nEnzyme differentiates the Newton iterates and Optimistix applies the implicit-function\ntheorem at its own stopping point. Newton converges quadratically, so both land on the\nsolution to rounding and the gradients agree closely.\n\n::: {#7d71542d .cell execution_count=2}\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=2}\n```{=html}\n<style type=\"text/css\">\n</style>\n<table id=\"T_e27aa\">\n  <thead>\n    <tr>\n      <th id=\"T_e27aa_level0_col0\" class=\"col_heading level0 col0\" >implementation</th>\n      <th id=\"T_e27aa_level0_col1\" class=\"col_heading level0 col1\" >‖g‖₂</th>\n      <th id=\"T_e27aa_level0_col2\" class=\"col_heading level0 col2\" >max rel. diff vs enzyme</th>\n    </tr>\n  </thead>\n  <tbody>\n    <tr>\n      <td id=\"T_e27aa_row0_col0\" class=\"data row0 col0\" >enzyme</td>\n      <td id=\"T_e27aa_row0_col1\" class=\"data row0 col1\" >0.737983</td>\n      <td id=\"T_e27aa_row0_col2\" class=\"data row0 col2\" >0.0e+00</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td id=\"T_e27aa_row1_col0\" class=\"data row1 col0\" >jax</td>\n      <td id=\"T_e27aa_row1_col1\" class=\"data row1 col1\" >0.737983</td>\n      <td id=\"T_e27aa_row1_col2\" class=\"data row1 col2\" >1.4e-14</td>\n    </tr>\n  </tbody>\n</table>\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n## Timings\n\nFloat64, median of 3–10 runs after warm-up. \"Forward\" is the converged Newton solve;\nfor JAX that is the `while_loop` version.\n\n::: {#fba03443 .cell execution_count=3}\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display}\n```{=html}\n<div style=\"height:525px; width:100%;\">            <script src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/mathjax/3.2.2/es5/tex-svg.min.js\"></script><script>if (window.MathJax && window.MathJax.Hub && window.MathJax.Hub.Config) {window.MathJax.Hub.Config({SVG: {font: \"STIX-Web\"}});}</script>                <script>window.PlotlyConfig = {MathJaxConfig: 'local'};</script>\n        <script charset=\"utf-8\" src=\"https://cdn.plot.ly/plotly-4.1.1.min.js\" integrity=\"sha256-O24V1F27f8pb0glCkelh3cVHLNiHAJ5gCaVtq2aNch8=\" crossorigin=\"anonymous\"></script>                <div id=\"1d067f37-63ff-48c6-8d54-cd62996ff2cb\" class=\"plotly-graph-div\" style=\"height:100%; width:100%;\"></div>            <script>                window.PLOTLYENV=window.PLOTLYENV || {};     